SUMMARY:Historical Society of Ottawa - 20th Century Canadian History Through the Magic of Radio
DESCRIPTION:Guest Speaker: Laurence Wall\, Retired CBC Ottawa Radio News Announcer\nDetails\nLaurence Wall looks back at the great events of the last century that radio helped bring to life.  was “the voice of the National Research time signal”. His 44-year career with the CBC included presenting the news to loyal CBC Ottawa radio listeners for close to three decades – totalling more than 50\,000 newscasts and updates. \nAdmission is free. All are welcome to attend. \n 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/historical-society-of-ottawa-20th-century-canadian-history-through-the-magic-of-radio/
LOCATION:Ottawa Public Library\, Main Branch\, 120 Metcalfe St.\, Ottawa\, Ontario\, K1P 5M2\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="The Historical Society of Ottawa":MAILTO:info@historicalsocietyottawa.ca
GEO:45.420388;-75.6954878
